{"id":17998,"slug":"the-fugitive-kind","title":"The Fugitive Kind","year":1960,"country":"United States","duration":121,"spine":515,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/17998-the-fugitive-kind","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/54bc36388e16357fc3a1d942cb8d5b1f/gxZAPSOZS3yNklK8cd2gjlpnpKsGFq_large.jpg","description":"\nFour Oscar-winning actors—Marlon Brando, Anna Magnani, Joanne Woodward, and Maureen Stapleton—shine in this enthralling film, which also brings together the legendary talents of director Sidney Lumet and writer Tennessee Williams. A smoldering, snakeskin-jacketed Brando is Val Xavier, a drifter trying to go straight. He finds work and solace in a small-town southern variety store run by the married, sexually frustrated Lady Torrance (Magnani), who proves as much a temptation for Val as does local wild child Carol Cutrere (Woodward). Lumet captures the intense, fearless performances and Williams’s hot-blooded story­telling and social critique with his customary restraint, resulting in a drama of uncommon sophistication and craft.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Sidney Lumet","slug":"sidney-lumet"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Marlon Brando","role":"Valentine “Snakeskin” Xavier","slug":"marlon-brando"},{"actor":"Anna Magnani","role":"Lady Torrance","slug":"anna-magnani"},{"actor":"Joanne Woodward","role":"Carol Cutrere","slug":"joanne-woodward"},{"actor":"Maureen Stapleton","role":"Vee Talbot","slug":"maureen-stapleton"},{"actor":"Victor Jory","role":"Jabe Torrance","slug":"victor-jory"},{"actor":"R. G. Armstrong","role":"Sheriff Jordan Talbot","slug":"r-g-armstrong"},{"actor":"John Baragrey","role":"David Cutrere","slug":"john-baragrey"},{"actor":"Virgilia Chew","role":"Nurse Porter","slug":"virgilia-chew"},{"actor":"Sally Gracie","role":"Dolly Hamma","slug":"sally-gracie"},{"actor":"Ben Yaffee","role":"Dog Hamma","slug":"ben-yaffee"},{"actor":"Lucille Benson","role":"Beulah Binnings","slug":"lucille-benson"},{"actor":"J